<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">stand</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">stand</ansi> command allows you to forcefully stand up when you've been knocked
to the ground (<ansi fg="red">prone</ansi>), guaranteed to succeed but at a significant stamina cost.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must be prone (knocked down)
  - Must have at least 15% of maximum stamina

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">stand</ansi>
  Stand up immediately, bypassing automatic recovery

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Stamina Cost:</ansi> 15% of your maximum stamina
  <ansi fg="stat">Success Rate:</ansi> 100% (guaranteed, unlike automatic recovery)
  <ansi fg="stat">Action Cost:</ansi> Uses your action for the current round

<ansi fg="yellow">Automatic Recovery:</ansi>

If you don't manually stand, you will <ansi fg="yellow">automatically attempt</ansi> to recover each round
after the minimum prone duration expires:

  - <ansi fg="stat">Minimum Duration:</ansi> Must remain prone for 1 full round
  - <ansi fg="stat">Recovery Chance:</ansi> Based on your Dexterity stat
    - 25 Dexterity = 25% chance per round
    - 100 Dexterity = 53% chance per round
    - 300 Dexterity = 75% chance per round
  - <ansi fg="stat">Recovery Penalty:</ansi> Only 1 attack that round (struggling to stand)

<ansi fg="yellow">Strategy:</ansi>

Use <ansi fg="command">stand</ansi> when you MUST get up immediately and have stamina to spare.
Otherwise, save stamina and let automatic recovery handle it - you'll still get 1 attack
while trying to stand.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help bash</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help trip</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help kick</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>
